  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life saving gender&#x2013;based violence and sexual and reproductive health services for Sudanese new arrivals in Egypt and host communities affected by the Sudan crisis through Women and Girls Safe Spaces in Aswan and Greater Cairo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project enhances the provision of Minimum Initial Services Package (MISP) for SRH in crisis with a focus on providing integrated GBV-SRH service for refugees and host community members affected by Sudan crisis. The project aims to increase the presence of and access to GBV prevention and response services through 6 Women and Girls Safe Spaces (WGSS) in Greater Cairo (4) and Aswan (2). The WGSSs function as a hub for the delivery of and referral to GBV-SRH services in coordination with other protection and health partners. The project targets 8,000 affected people with its Protection-GBV engagement and 2,000 with Health-SRH activities.</narrative>
  </description>
